From 63b6843c4c7f5c4040da5d0dfbc87d36c6c9ffe6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: suiyan <suiyan@sunmmio.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 17:57:53 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] target/dadao: advance env->pc for DISAS_TOO_MANY before TB
 lookup (ML-003f)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Only branch-family instructions (br*/jump/call/ret) write env->pc via
tcg_gen_st_i64; dadao_tr_tb_stop()'s DISAS_TOO_MANY case called
tcg_gen_lookup_and_goto_ptr() (which resolves the next TB from
env->pc via cpu_get_tb_cpu_state()) without ever advancing env->pc for
a TB that ends without executing a branch.

This is invisible for ordinary multi-instruction TBs (they almost
always end on a real branch in practice), but cpu_io_recompile()
constructs single-instruction "precise IO" TBs for whatever
non-branch instruction triggered the mid-block MMIO/IO access — for
those, DISAS_TOO_MANY fires after exactly one non-branch instruction,
env->pc is never touched, and the next-TB lookup resolves back to the
exact same stale PC: an infinite re-translate/re-execute loop of that
one instruction (observed as unbounded `cpu_io_recompile: rewound
execution of TB to <same pc>` — verified stuck for 60s+, not merely
slow).

Fix: write env->pc = ctx->base.pc_next before the goto-ptr lookup in
the DISAS_TOO_MANY case, mirroring what every branch instruction
already does explicitly.

Verified: a previously-hanging picolibc printf link (indirect call
through stdout's tinystdio put callback, a non-branch load instruction
was the repeating PC) now completes instead of hanging past a 60s
timeout. E2E 27/27, differential AGREE(4-way)=200/DIVERGE=0, no
regression (ordinary TBs already ending on real branches are
unaffected).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 target/dadao/translate.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/target/dadao/translate.c b/target/dadao/translate.c
index 789dcaf..3e9ca95 100644
--- a/target/dadao/translate.c
+++ b/target/dadao/translate.c
@@ -1341,6 +1341,18 @@ static void dadao_tr_tb_stop(DisasContextBase *dcbase, CPUState *cpu)
 
     switch (ctx->base.is_jmp) {
     case DISAS_TOO_MANY:
+        /* Falling off the end of the TB (max_insns / page boundary / a
+         * single-instruction TB forced by cpu_io_recompile) — unlike every
+         * branch-family instruction, plain sequential insns never write
+         * env->pc themselves. tcg_gen_lookup_and_goto_ptr() finds the next
+         * TB via cpu_get_tb_cpu_state(), which reads env->pc directly, so
+         * it must be advanced to pc_next here or the lookup resolves back
+         * to this same (stale) PC — infinite re-translation/re-execution
+         * loop of the same instruction (only ever bites single-instruction
+         * non-branch TBs, e.g. the ones cpu_io_recompile constructs).
+         */
+        tcg_gen_st_i64(tcg_constant_i64(ctx->base.pc_next), tcg_env,
+                       offsetof(CPUDADAOState, pc));
         tcg_gen_lookup_and_goto_ptr();
         break;
     case DISAS_NORETURN:
-- 
